e will add an endpoint in `,jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"foo.ts"})," ","that calls our other service."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["When you’re done, press ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Check"})," to see if you got it right."]})]}),onCheck:rd,bonus:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("p",{children:"Encore is not opinionated about monoliths vs. microservices, but lets you build microservices with a monolith-like developer experience. For instance, you get IDE auto-complete and cross-service type-safety for API calls."}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("p",{children:"When deploying to the cloud, Encore lets you choose between combining services into one process or keeping them separate. This is useful for improved efficiency at smaller scales, and for co-locating services for increased performance."})]}),solution:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("div",{className:"-mt-6",children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["To create an Encore service, add a file named ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"encore.service.ts"})," in a directory. The file must export a service instance, by calling"," ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"new Service"}),", imported from",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"encore.dev/service"}),". For example:"]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeSnippet$1,{title:"Service definition example",value:getPartOfContent(codeContent$2,void 0,!0)})]})})]})},creatingServicesLesson={title:"Creating services",slug:"service-create",page:CreatingServicesLesson},codeContent$1=`//-- import
import { api } from "encore.dev/api";
import { hello } from "~encore/clients";
//-- import

//-- response
interface Response {
  greeting: string;
}
//-- response

//-- handler
export const greeting = api(
  { expose: true, method: "GET", path: "/greeting/:name" },
  async ({ name }: { name: string }): Promise<Response> => {
    // Calling the get endpoint on the hello service
    const { message } = await hello.get();

    return { greeting: \`\${message} \${name}!\` };
  },
);
//-- handler
`;HighlightJS.registerLanguage("js",javascript);const ServicesCallingLesson=({lesson:td,group:ed})=>{const{meta:nd}=useProcessUpdate(),rd="foo/foo.ts";reactExports.useEffect(()=>{HighlightJS.highlightAll()},[]);const sd=()=>{if(!nd)return!1;const{pkgs:od}=nd;return od.some(cd=>cd.rpc_calls.length)};return jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(LessonIntro,{group:ed,lesson:td,children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("p",{children:"With Encore.ts, calling another service is just like calling a local function, with complete type-safety. Under the hood, Encore.ts will translate this function call into an actual service-to-service HTTP call, resulting in trace data being generated for each call."}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["When compiling your application, Encore uses static analysis to parse all APIs and make then available through the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"~encore/clients"})," module for internal calls."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(DocsLink,{title:"API calls docs",href:"https://encore.dev/docs/ts/primitives/api-calls"})]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeTaskInstructions,{lesson:td,group:ed,title:jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("span",{children:["Add an endpoint to ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(OpenFileInEditor,{path:rd})," that calls the hello service"]})}),description:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["To implement an endpoint, first import the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"api"})," function from the"," ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"encore.dev/api"})," module. We also want to import the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"hello"})," ","service from the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"~encore/clients"})," module."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeSnippet$1,{title:"Import statement",value:getPartOfContent(codeContent$1,"import")}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("p",{children:"Define the type that will get returned from the endpoint."}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeSnippet$1,{title:"API response type",value:getPartOfContent(codeContent$1,"response")}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["This time, let's make use of a dynamic path parameter in the path. The path parameter"," ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:":name"})," will be inputted as an argument to our endpoint function. Inside the endpoint function we call the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"get"})," method on the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"hello"})," ","service and await the result. We then concatenate the result with the"," ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"name"})," parameter and return the full greeting."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeSnippet$1,{title:"Endpoint handler",value:getPartOfContent(codeContent$1,"handler")}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["When you’re done, press ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Check"})," to see if you got it right."]})]}),onCheck:sd,bonus:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["Go to the"," ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(Link,{to:"../../flow",className:"link-brandient",children:"Flow"})," ","page to view an up-to-date architectural diagram of your application. You should see that the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"foo"})," service is calling the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"hello"})," service."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("p",{children:"Flow is designed to help you reason about your service architecture and identify which services depend on each other and how they work together."})]}),solution:jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeSnippet$1,{title:"Service-to-service call example",value:getPartOfContent(codeContent$1,void 0)})})]})},servicesCallingLesson={title:"Calling another service",slug:"service-call",page:ServicesCallingLesson},codeContent=`import { describe, expect, test } from "vitest";
import { greeting } from "./foo";

describe("greeting", () => {
  test("should combine string with parameter value", async () => {
    // Call the greeting endpoint like an ordinary function
    const resp = await greeting({ name: "world" });

    expect(resp.greeting).toBe("Hello world!");
  });
});
`,TestAPIsLesson=({lesson:td,group:ed})=>{const nd="foo/foo.ts",rd=()=>!0;return jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(LessonIntro,{group:ed,lesson:td,children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("p",{children:"Encore provides a suite of built-in tooling to simplify testing your application."}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(DocsLink,{title:"Automated testing docs",href:"https://encore.dev/docs/ts/develop/testing"})]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeTaskInstructions,{lesson:td,group:ed,title:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("span",{children:["Add a test for ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(OpenFileInEditor,{path:nd})]}),description:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:['Create a new file in the "foo" service and name it ',jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"foo.test.ts"}),"."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["Using Vitest, write a test that verifies the behavior of the ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"greeting"})," ","endpoint."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(CodeSnippet$1,{title:"Unit test",value:getPartOfContent(codeContent,void 0)}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["To run the test, execute ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"encore test"})," in your terminal in the root of your application. The ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("code",{children:"encore test"})," command sets up all the necessary infrastructure in test mode before handing over to the test runner."]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsx(BashPrompt,{lines:["encore test"]}),jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs("p",{children:["When you can see that the test is passing press"," ",jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("span",{className:"font-semibold",children:"Done"})," to finish the lesson."]})]}),buttonText:"Done",onCheck:rd,bonus:jsxRuntimeExports.jsxs(jsxRuntimeExports.Fragment,{children:[jsxRuntimeExports.jsx("p",{children:"Since Encore removes almost all boilerplate, most of the code you write is business logic that involves databases and calling APIs between ser